[2026-03-04T20:07:27.161Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwModQZ8y4XU6QKuHtGMdS","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# app-building\n     2→\n     3→Simple and extensible platform for dark factory agentic app building: creating apps\n     4→according to a spec without human involvement along the way. Example use cases:\n     5→\n     6→* `npm run agent -- -p \"Build me an app XYZ based on this spec: ...\"`\n     7→* `npm run agent -- -p \"Continue maintaining app XYZ and fix these bugs: ...\"`\n     8→* `npm run agent -- -i` for interactive access to the agent.\n     9→\n    10→Core ideas:\n    11→\n    12→* The agent runs within a docker container that clones a repo and exposes an HTTP server for control.\n    13→* The agent builds by following a set of skill documents with guides\n    14→  for breaking its work down into tasks and directives for performing those tasks.\n    15→* The agent commits logs for it to review later and improve its skills.\n    16→* All code changes are committed and pushed back to the remote from inside the container.\n    17→\n    18→Containers can run locally or remotely.\n    19→\n    20→## Setup\n    21→\n    22→```bash\n    23→npm install\n    24→```\n    25→\n    26→Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in all required API keys.\n    27→\n    28→## Running the Agent\n    29→\n    30→`npm run agent` starts a new container with the running agent. By default the container is local, add `--remote` to spawn the container remotely. This requires FLY_API_TOKEN in .env\n    31→\n    32→### Detached mode\n    33→\n    34→```bash\n    35→npm run agent\n    36→npm run agent -- -p \"<prompt>\"\n    37→npm run agent -- --branch dev --push-branch feature/xyz -p \"<prompt>\"\n    38→```\n    39→\n    40→Starts a container, optionally queues a prompt, then detaches. The container processes the prompt followed by any pending tasks, commits and pushes results, then exits.\n    41→\n    42→### Interactive mode\n    43→\n    44→```bash\n    45→npm run agent -- -i\n    46→```\n    47→\n    48→Chat with the agent inside a container. Output is streamed via event polling. Press ESC to interrupt the current message. On exit, the container is detached and finishes any remaining work.\n    49→\n    50→### Checking status\n    51→\n    52→```bash\n    53→npm run status\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→Connects to the running container's HTTP API and shows state, revision, queue depth, cost, and recent log output. Tails logs in real-time (Ctrl+C to stop). Errors if no agent is running.\n    57→\n    58→### Stopping the agent\n    59→\n    60→```bash\n    61→npm run stop\n    62→npm run stop -- <containerName>\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→Sends an HTTP stop signal. Without arguments, finds and stops all running containers. Pass a container name to stop a specific one.\n    66→\n    67→## Skills\n    68→\n    69→The provided skill documents emphasize a structured approach for autonomously building\n    70→high quality, well tested apps from the initial spec. During the initial app build\n    71→it does the following:\n    72→\n    73→1. Designs a comprehensive test specification based on the initial spec.\n    74→2. Builds the app and writes tests to match the spec.\n    75→3. Gets all the tests to pass, deploys to production, and does further testing.\n    76→\n    77→The initial build will not come out perfect. The agent can followup with maintenance passes\n    78→where it checks to make sure it closely followed the spec and skill directives and fixes\n    79→any issues it finds. It will also fix reported bugs and update the skills to avoid\n    80→similar problems in the future.\n    81→\n    82→As long as each individual step the agent takes is within its capabilities (it can usually\n    83→do it but not always) the agent will converge on an app that follows the initial spec\n    84→and skill directives.\n    85→\n    86→Key things to watch out for:\n    87→\n    88→* Best suited for CRUD and API-calling apps up to a medium level of complexity.\n    89→  Overly complicated or specialized apps will not work as well yet.\n    90→* Make sure to get a Replay API key and configure it. The agent will use Replay to identify\n    91→  and debug problems it encounters in tests or the deployed app.\n    92→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012BcyZmNrKdFi6frwYnSbba","session_id":"7c97f9f9-38f7-47f6-b325-4f48ece0a82a","uuid":"cb077dde-bb1b-4067-a08f-8aa464ab347b"}
